# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 2: fair_price), edited.

~ baltus_start
Narrator: The Trading Post smells of tallow and damp wool, a brass scale gleaming on the counter.
baltus_tolliver [weary]: Eleanor Heyling sells fine rag paper across the Round for less than the mill charges. Glance at her ledger and see how she keeps her purse full.
* We will look -> baltus_accept
* Not our business -> END

~ baltus_accept
baltus_tolliver [smile]: Boundlessly grateful. A quiet look at her columns is all a fair man asks.
quest a_fair_price asked
set price_asked
-> END

~ eleanor_visit
Narrator: Dry parchment and walnut gall scent the shelves, an open account book beside Eleanor's elbow.
eleanor_heyling [neutral]: If Baltus sent you to whine about vellum, tell him to scrape the lead from under his brass scale first. Come to read, or just to hover?
* [Investigation DC 12] Study her ledger over her shoulder -> ledger_ok | ledger_fail
* Ask her side of it -> eleanor_side
* Leave -> END

~ eleanor_side
eleanor_heyling [angry]: A pound of his lampblack ink weighs fourteen ounces by honest iron. I price my sheets so the schoolhouse needn't beg him for scraps.
-> eleanor_visit

~ ledger_ok
Narrator: {name} traces the red margin ink: a newcomer fund signed by Finneas Trout covers the loss on every quire.
eleanor_heyling [sly]: Sharp eyes. Finneas and I see to it our people have paper without paying a tithe to the Old Ways.
set price_ledger_seen
-> END

~ ledger_fail
Narrator: Her hand drops flat over the page before {name} can make sense of the cramped figures.
eleanor_heyling [neutral]: This book is not for sale. If you want sums, bother Tamsin Ledger at the Mayor's House.
-> END

~ tamsin_audit
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Two merchants arguing arithmetic is Wickermoor's dullest sin. For ten gold in candles, I will audit both books before the sixth bell.
* Pay ten gold -> audit_paid
* Another way -> END

~ audit_paid
gold -10
Narrator: By next candle-mark, Tamsin lays down a single sheet of foolscap, smelling of cold tea.
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Baltus thumbs his brass pan by two drams; Eleanor covers her cheap paper with a schoolhouse grant from Finneas Trout. Both books balance, if you squint.
set price_ledger_seen
-> END

~ broker
baltus_tolliver [sly]: You look like folks who have seen the bottom of the inkwell. How do we settle our dear neighbour?
* Broker a truce -> truce
* Tell Baltus where her money comes from -> side_baltus
* Tell Eleanor his scale is rigged -> side_eleanor

~ truce
baltus_tolliver [neutral]: Let her hear your proposal, then, though I doubt city ears take kindly to country sense.
* [Persuasion DC 13] Argue a fair price for both -> truce_ok | truce_fail

~ truce_ok
baltus_tolliver [smile]: Paper to her shelves, ink to mine, and no more bleeding the penny tray. I can live with that.
eleanor_heyling [neutral]: So long as your weights stay honest, Mr. Tolliver, we have an accord.
set price_outcome = "truce"
quest a_fair_price done
gold +30
standing cult +1
standing newcomers +1
-> END

~ truce_fail
eleanor_heyling [angry]: I will not take lectures on fairness from a man with a heavy thumb.
baltus_tolliver [weary]: You see how she is, friends.
-> broker

~ side_baltus
baltus_tolliver [sly]: A schoolhouse grant from Finneas? Wait till the Round hears the newcomers need charity just to write a letter.
set price_outcome = "baltus"
quest a_fair_price done
gold +25
standing cult +1
standing newcomers -1
-> END

~ side_eleanor
eleanor_heyling [smile]: Two drams of lead under the pan, tested in front of the whole Round. Look how red his ears are.
set price_outcome = "eleanor"
quest a_fair_price done
gold +25
standing cult -1
standing newcomers +1
-> END
